# Merge drivers, chosen per file by what the file *is* rather than by what is
# convenient.
#
# The first port merge in this project produced exactly one conflict, and it was
# not in application code: three agents had each called the Jev client, and the
# client appends a row to this log as a side effect. Because every row goes on the
# end of the same file, three branches appending at once conflict textually even
# though no row contradicts another.
#
# That is not a one-off. Every one of the ~100 workflows runs a Jev gate, so every
# one of them appends here. Left to the default driver, the audit log alone would
# have produced a conflict on almost every merge - which is precisely the class of
# problem the plugin host was built to remove, reappearing in a file nobody
# thought of as contended.
#
# `union` is the correct driver for an append-only log: it concatenates both sides
# and never emits a conflict marker. No row is lost and none is invented. Each row
# carries its own `audit_id` and `decided_at`, so the merged file stays a complete
# and unambiguous record regardless of the order rows end up in.
orchestration/decisions/*.jsonl merge=union

# Same reasoning, one file per workflow. The port briefs and the program audit are
# append-only Markdown: a new section is added, never an old one rewritten, so a
# union merge preserves both sides' text instead of interleaving it.
orchestration/PROGRAM-AUDIT.md merge=union
